IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa22-part30`

-- coa22-tests-part30.l4: tests for Part 30 (ss 994 to 999). Every expected value below was decided from the text
-- (quoted in coa22-part30.l4) before the run and is written beside the assertion; none was copied from the output.
-- Each test says which way the case falls: T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING ("not covered").
-- A trace is not an assertion on the stable binary: each #TRACE carries its expected outcome on the line before it
-- (-- EXPECT:), and check-traces.py compares it with what the binary prints.

§ `Part 30 tests`

§§ `s 994 Petition by company member`

-- (1A) a removal of the auditor on either ground is treated as prejudicial to some part of the members
#ASSERT `s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- removed, but on neither ground: the text deems nothing
#ASSERT `s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not removed at all
#ASSERT `s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) a transferee by operation of law is treated as a member; any other non-member is not covered
#ASSERT `s 994(2) the person who is not a member is treated as a member for the purposes of Part 30` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(2) the person who is not a member is treated as a member for the purposes of Part 30` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) "company" means a company within the meaning of the Act (a "means" definition: no is the text's own)
#ASSERT `s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(a) args: prejudicial to members generally, to some part, that part includes the petitioner, (1A) answer
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- some part of the members, but not including the petitioner: outside "(including at least himself)"
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the petitioner is in a part, but nothing is prejudicial
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A) supplies the prejudice to a part; the petitioner must still be in it
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(b)
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(b) the ground of an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is made out` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 994(1)(b) the ground of an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is made out` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1) args: s 112 member, (2) treated as member, (3) company, ground (a), ground (b)
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ground (b) alone is enough
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a member (s 112 says no) but a transferee by operation of law
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a member and not a transferee: the text is silent
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a member with no ground made out
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the body is not a company within the meaning of the Act: "company" means only that
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the company seam is open (points outside the text)
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the membership seam is open and (2) does not help
#ASSERT `s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 995 Petition by Secretary of State`

-- (1) each of the four routes, and none (args: s 437 report; ss 447/448 powers; FSMA Part 11 powers; investigator report)
#ASSERT `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) "company" means a body corporate liable to be wound up under the 1986 Act or the 1989 Order
#ASSERT `s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) args: (1) applies, (4) company, it appears (a), it appears (b)
#ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- it does not appear to him: the "If" fails
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading is JUST FALSE, fork F16); the facts are unchanged
#ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the section does not apply to the company on the facts: not covered
#ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a company within subsection (4)
#ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) in addition to, or instead of, a winding-up petition: the same answer either way
#ASSERT `s 995(3) the Secretary of State may petition under Part 30 whether or not he has presented a winding-up petition` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(3) the Secretary of State may petition under Part 30 whether or not he has presented a winding-up petition` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 995(3) the Secretary of State may petition under Part 30 whether or not he has presented a winding-up petition` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 995(3) the Secretary of State may petition under Part 30 whether or not he has presented a winding-up petition` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 996 Powers of the court under this Part`

#ASSERT `s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading is JUST FALSE, fork F17); the facts are unchanged
#ASSERT `s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) all five kinds, and any other, are within (1)
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2)(b)(i) require the company to refrain from doing or continuing an act complained of` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2)(b)(ii) require the company to do an act that the petitioner has complained it has omitted to do` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2)(c) authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name and on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2)(d) require the company not to make any, or any specified, alterations in its articles without the leave of the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2)(e) provide for the purchase of the shares of any members of the company by other members or by the company itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST TRUE) `s 996(2) any other provision for giving relief under subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- where the court is not satisfied, (1) gives no power, so (2) adds none
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST FALSE) `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading is JUST FALSE, fork F18); the facts are unchanged
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` (JUST FALSE) `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` NOTHING `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(e) reduction of capital accordingly only in the case of a purchase by the company itself
#ASSERT `s 996(2)(e) the order provides for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 996(2)(e) the order provides for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 997 Application of general rule-making powers`
-- Inert (reason 2: rule-making power); nothing to test. See NOTES.md.

§§ `s 998 Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar`

-- (1) args: the order alters the constitution; it gives leave to alter it
#ASSERT `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) 14 days from the order; a longer period only if the court allowed one and it is longer than 14
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the date a number of days after the date of an event` (Date 1 1 2026) 14 EQUALS Date 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the date a number of days after the date of an event` (Date 25 1 2026) 14 EQUALS Date 8 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the date a number of days after the date of an event` (Date 25 12 2026) 14 EQUALS Date 8 1 2027
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` NOTHING EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` (JUST 28) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` (JUST 14) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` (JUST 10) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` (JUST 15) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST 28) EQUALS Date 29 1 2026
-- args: order made, longer period, date delivered. The last day itself is in time; the next day is not.
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar within the time allowed` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar within the time allowed` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar within the time allowed` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar within the time allowed` (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST 28) (Date 29 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(2) the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar within the time allowed` (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST 28) (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- the regulative rule: the company MUST deliver WITHIN the days allowed (the clock counts days from the order)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE FALSE NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 998 deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 14
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE FALSE NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 998 deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 15
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` FALSE TRUE NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- the court allowed 28 days: day 28 is in time
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE FALSE (JUST 28) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 998 deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 28
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` TRUE FALSE (JUST 28) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 998 deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` AT 29
-- the order neither alters the constitution nor gives leave: there is no duty
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` FALSE FALSE NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- (3) default derived from (1) and (2); args: alters, leave, order made, longer period, date delivered (if), date asked about
-- no duty, so no default
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- duty, still within the 14 days, not yet delivered: no default yet
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- duty, 16 January, not delivered: default
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 16 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- delivered on time
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 1 2026)) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 1 2026)) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- delivered late
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 16 1 2026)) (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the court allowed 28 days: on 20 January the company is still in time; on 30 January it is not
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST 28) NOTHING (Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST 28) NOTHING (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (3) the offence: the company, and every officer in default. args: default; officer; s 1121 answer
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an officer whom section 1121 does not find in default: not named by the text, so not covered (marginal reading)
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- not an officer
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no default by the company: "If a company makes default" fails
#ASSERT `s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4) the penalty, written from the text: summary conviction; level 3; daily default fine one-tenth of level 3; no imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 998` EQUALS Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)), (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)), FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 998(4) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 998` EQUALS Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)), NOTHING, FALSE)

§§ `s 999 Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered`

#ASSERT `s 999(1) section 999 applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(1) section 999 applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(a) args: (1) applies; the order amends the articles
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(b) args: (1) applies; the order amends a resolution or agreement; Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to it (s 29)
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) args: (1) applies; the copy is issued after the order is made; the effect of the order is incorporated into the articles
#ASSERT `s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment
#ASSERT `s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a copy issued before the order was made is outside "after the order is made"
#ASSERT `s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) default derived; args: (2)(a) answer, accompanied (a); (2)(b) answer, accompanied (b); (3) answer, accompanied (3)
#ASSERT `s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- every requirement that applies was met
#ASSERT `s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no requirement applies
#ASSERT `s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) the offence (shadow directors are not mentioned in this section)
#ASSERT `s 999(4)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(4)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 999(4)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 999(4)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 999(4)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (5) level 3 on the standard scale on summary conviction, and no daily default fine
#ASSERT `s 999(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 999` EQUALS Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)), NOTHING, FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 999(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 999` EQUALS `s 998(4) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 998`)

§§ `The conversion of a fine limit into pounds (not a provision)`

-- args: the fine limit; the pounds a level stands for (here 1,000, an arbitrary test figure, not the Act's); the statutory maximum in pounds (here 5,000, likewise)
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 0.2)) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (JUST (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` 750)) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` (JUST `a fine without a stated limit`) 1000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` NOTHING 1000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING





-- assertions written 128; satisfied 128 (stable 1.6.110 and 1.6.109, check.sh)
